From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI: the ground behind the notifications is white

Measured on the device on 2026-10-27, on V89, by scanning the rows of a raw
framebuffer grab. With three notifications in the shade, two bands of grey 238
run the full width of the screen, 1072 x 8 px each, at the 4dp gaps patch 0059
put between the cards (y 766-773 and 947-954). The same band appears in the
quick settings view, 1072 x 8 px at y 693-700, and it is the only grey of any
size left there.

It is `notification_shade_background_color`, #EEEEEE, which
NotificationStackScrollLayout paints behind the stack
(NotificationStackScrollLayout.java:405). The cards are white and cover it, so
it shows only in the gaps, and the shade below the last card is the window's
own white -- which is why the two do not match.

Rule 1 of docs/design/eink-ui.md names #EEEEEE as a colour that lands on panel
level 14 and cannot mark a region here. Nothing is lost by making it white: the
cards are told apart by the 2 px black outline patch 0059 gave them, which is
what rule 3 asks for, and the grey was never doing that work.

A value in SystemUI, not in framework-res: SystemUI's resources are its own
APK's, so com.android.internal.R, framework.jar and the 45 ART boot files are
untouched either way, and this is where the colour is defined.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/values/colors.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/values/colors.xml
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@
     <color name="notification_divider_color">#FF616161</color>
 
     <!-- The background color of the notification shade -->
-    <color name="notification_shade_background_color">#ffeeeeee</color>
+    <color name="notification_shade_background_color">#ffffffff</color>
 
     <!-- The color of the ripples on the untinted notifications -->
     <color name="notification_ripple_untinted_color">#28000000</color>
